  "title": "Xu Guangqi",
  "summary": "Xu Guangqi, born in Shanghai, was a Ming official who worked with Matteo Ricci on a Chinese translation of the first six books of Euclid's Elements, published in 1607. He compiled the agricultural treatise Nongzheng quanshu and from 1629 until his death led a calendar reform with Jesuit help.",
